│  ### I. AGENT PRIORITY HIERARCHY 🔴 SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE FIX                  │
│                                                                              │
│  | Current (BUG) | Correct Hierarchy |                                       │
│  |---|---|                                                                   │
│  | Regime Agent > **Entry Gate** ❌ | **Entry Gate** > Regime Agent |        │
│  | Gate says UNKNOWN → proceed anyway ❌ | Gate says UNKNOWN → **BLOCK** |   │
│  | Regime Agent authorizes override ❌ | Gate is **SOLE gatekeeper** |       │
│                                                                              │
│  **Entry Gate is the GATEKEEPER** — if it returns UNKNOWN with 0             │
│  confidence, NO further agents should proceed. Regime Agent provides         │
│  context but **CANNOT authorize** a trade the Gate rejected. This hierarchy  │
│  must be enforced at the orchestration layer.                                │
